<br class="Apple-interchange-newline"></p><p><br></p><p>1.Open Permit to Work for P-5740 Performance Test<br>2.Check Firewater package condition to ensure equipment readiness according to ART-OPS-ME-002 check list section 1-4 “Check list BEFORE startup”<br>3.Close Firewater ring main Isolation valve Tag. No. HV-3663 (Dwg.A-1-PP-PR-06-0440)<br>4.Start P-5740 firewater pump<br>5.Perform Firewater pump operational check according to ART-OPS-ME-002 check list section 5-8 “Check list DURING pump operating”<br>6.Record Vibration by Microlog Analyzer at Operating condition<br>7.Fully open manual shutoff valve Tag. No. HV-3656 (Dwg.A-1-PP-PR-06-0440)<br>8.Fully open manual control valve Tag. No. HV-3655 (Dwg.A-1-PP-PR-06-0440)<br>9.Fully close pressure control valve Tag. No. PCV-5740 (Dwg.A-1-PP-PR-06-0440)<br>10.Fully close manual shutoff valve Tag. No. HV-3649 (Dwg.A-1-PP-PR-06-0440)<br>11.Record all data on Maximum flow condition according to P-5740 APP Operational Test Data Sheet as followings<br>• Record pressure on PIT-5740<br>• Record flow rate on FG-5740<br>• Record Engine speed on Engine control panel<br>• Record Engine cooling water pressure PG-5743<br>• Record Engine lube oil pressure on PG-5742<br>• Record Engine cooling water temperature on TG-5741<br>12.Gradually increase header pressure by closing manual control valve Tag. No.HV-3655 about 1 bar. at a time.<br>13.Repeat step 11and 12 until pump discharge PIT-5740 reached 11.2barg.<br>14.Open manual control valve Tag. No.HV-3655 (avoiding running on Shutoff Head condition)<br>15.Stop P-5740 Firewater pump.<br>16.Normalizing P-5740 Firewater Pump system<br>17.Closed Permit to Work for P-5740 Performance Test.</p>', NULL, '2025-05-25 18:37:43', '2025-05-26 17:47:54', 'PTTEP\\Art.MechBC', 'PTTEP\\art.mechcrane', false, 'ART') RETURNING id INTO new_report_id;
