-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Checked final alignment. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Bump test thrust bearing clearance with E&amp;I team. (Ongoing)</p>  <p><b><u>LM2500 existing engine installation. </u></b>(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Applied final torque TMF bolt 21 ft/lbs. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installed turbine front frame support R&amp;L side and Applied torque 850 Nm. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Removed exhaust cone angle bar (L-shim). (Done)</p>  <p><b><u>Dry Gas Seal (NDE side) Replacement.</u></b> &nbsp;(80% progress)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Bump test thrust bearing clearance with E&amp;I team. (Ongoing)</p>  <p><b><u>Other Work</u></b></p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Reinstalled beam support for expansion joint replacement. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Repaired cladding of inlet plenum top side. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Remove special tools transfer beam between unit TEK-3200 and TEK-3300. (Done)</p>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <p><b>Night shift 30 Jan. 2025 activities.</b></p>  <p><b>PGT25 and DGS Exchange Jan 2025 activities. (92.5% Progress)</b></p>  <p><b><u>PGT25 Replacement.</u></b> &nbsp;(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Rechecked PGT-25 thrust bearing clearance. Final value = 0.56 mm.</p>  <p><b><u>LM2500 existing engine installation. </u></b>(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; •Reinstated piping and connections for gas turbine. (Ongoing)</p>  <p><b><u>Other Work</u></b></p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Performed battery limit de-isolation 5 points from total 7 points (remaining 12”/18” line).</p>  <p><b><u>Note;</u></b> please click in hyperlink for detail : </p>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <p><b>Day shift 31 Jan. 2025 activities.</b></p>  <p><b>PGT25 and DGS Exchange Jan 2025 activities. (95% Progress)</b></p>  <p><b><u>PGT25 Replacement.</u></b> &nbsp;(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Bump test thrust bearing clearance with E&amp;I team (Total clearance = 0.56 mm., Active side = 0.273 mm, In-Active side = -0.287 mm). (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Greased all exhaust cone support legs. (Done)</p>  <p><b><u>LM2500 existing engine installation. </u></b>(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Applied final torque air inlet duct 55-70 lb in. (6.22-7.91 N·m). (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installed the center body and apply final 55-70 lb in. (6.22-7.91 N·m).. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Calculated ignitor plugs for shim installation (Upper ignitor plug: No shims, Lower ignitor plug: 1 shims). (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; De-mechanical 6-inch outlet gas starter. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installed flexible cooling pipe. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Closed enclosure doors. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Finally checked engine instrument devices, F&amp;G devices, lighting, and CO2 nozzles by PFO2/NM-EI. (Ongoing)</p>  <p><b><u>Dry Gas Seal (NDE side) Replacement.</u></b> &nbsp;(90% progress)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Bump test thrust bearing clearance with E&amp;I team. (Total clearance = 0.30 mm., Active side = 0.15 mm, In-Active side = -0.15 mm). (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; De-isolated battery limit (compressor gas and seal gas). (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Dry gas seal leak test at 25 Bar. &nbsp;(Ongoing)</p>  <p><b><u>Other Work</u></b></p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Repaired cladding of exhaust plenum top side. (Done)</p>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <p><b>Night shift 31 Jan. 2025 activities.</b></p>  <p><b>PGT25 and DGS Exchange Jan 2025 activities. (96% Progress)</b></p>  <p><b><u>LM2500 existing engine installation. </u></b>(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Center body safety wire locking. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Final checked accessories and piping follow LM 2500 final check list. (Ongoing)</p>  <p><b><u>Install coupling spacer and coupling guard. </u></b>(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installed diaphragm pack and coupling spacer (Applied torque 90 Nm.). (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Coupling cover and bolts preparation. (Ongoing)</p>  <p><b><u>Other Work</u></b></p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Dry gas seal leak test by nitrogen with satisfactory results no internal passing and not found external leak at DGS piping flanges. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Opened PGT 25 capsule for cleaned capsule gasket and bolts. (Done)</p>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <p>Day shift 1 Feb. 2025 activities.</p>  <p><b>PGT25 and DGS Exchange Jan 2025 activities. (97% Progress)</b></p>  <p><b><u>PGT25 Replacement.</u></b> &nbsp;</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installed flexible hose return line at PGT25 oil galley. (Done)</p>  <p><b><u>LM2500 existing engine installation. </u></b>(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Final checked accessories and piping follow LM 2500 final check list. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Closed screen and door of air inlet plenum. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; De-self-isolation of synthetic engine lube oil 6 ea. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; De-processed isolation (fuel gas battery limit). (Pending)</p>  <p><b><u>Install coupling spacer and coupling guard. </u></b></p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installed coupling cover and lube oil piping. (Done)</p>  <p><b><u>Other Work</u></b></p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Performed LM2500 preservation by charge N2 about 1.5 psi. to the capsule. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Performed preservation on the old PGT-25 and closed the capsule ( Charge N2 about 3 psi.). &nbsp;(Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Fixed leak sight glass at lube oil compressor DE side. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Welding repair globe valve ¾ inch class 600 at seal gas line. (Ongoing)</p>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <p><b>Night shift 1 Feb. 2025 activities.</b></p>  <p><b>PGT25 and DGS Exchange Jan 2025 activities. (98% Progress)</b></p>  <p><b><u>LM2500 existing engine installation. </u></b>(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Cleaned inlet bell mount and air inlet screen. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Closed inlet screen and manhole of air inlet plenum. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Final cleaned inside LM 2500 enclosure. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; De-processed isolation (fuel gas battery limit). (Pending)</p>  <p>§&nbsp; Line 3"#600 at HP FUEL GAS K.O.DRUM</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Finally checked engine instrument devices by PFO2/NM-EI. (Ongoing)</p>  <p><b><u>PGT25 Replacement. </u></b>(Done) &nbsp;</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Applied RTV at support casing base. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Final cleaned at PGT 25 enclosure and below exhaust plenum. (Done)</p>  <p><b><u>Install coupling spacer and coupling guard. </u></b>(Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installed 3”#150 lube oil piping DE side. (Done)</p>  <p><b><u>Other Work</u></b></p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Replaced defective stud bolts at check valve 3-inch #150 for mineral LO system. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Reinstalled 11 Ea. deluge spray nozzles. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Fixed globe valve ¾ inch class 600 at seal gas line due to gas seeping. (Ongoing)</p>  <p>§&nbsp; Welding repair globe valve ¾ inch class 600 at seal gas line 2<sup>nd</sup> time.</p>  <p>§&nbsp; Reinstalled the valve and leak tested with N2 found at pressure 5 bar still seeping from locking bolts of valve body, not found seeping at valve bonnet (welding point repaired). &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>  <p>&nbsp;</p>  <p><b>Day shift 2 Feb. 2025 activities.</b></p>  <p><b>PGT25 and DGS Exchange Jan 2025 activities. (100% Progress and Waiting for start-up)</b></p>  <p><b><u>PGT25 Replacement.</u></b> &nbsp;</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Performed lined up mineral LO to all filters and checked for any leaks not found leak. (Done)</p>  <p><b><u>LM2500 existing engine installation. </u></b>(Ongoing)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Final checked Variable Stator Vane Actuating Mechanism and rigging. Found <b>fully open at -4 degrees</b> and <b>fully closed at 40 degrees. </b>(Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; De-processed isolation (fuel gas battery limit). (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Pressure tested and checked for any leaks in mechanical isolation flanges (Downstream KO drum HP FUEL GAS 3#300, and Outlet gas starter 6#150). No leaks found. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Finally checked engine instrument devices, F&amp;G devices, lighting, and CO2 nozzles by PFO2/NM-EI. (Done)</p>  <p><b><u>Install coupling spacer and coupling guard. </u></b></p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installed cover front side at compressor NDE. (Done)</p>  <p><b><u>Other Work</u></b></p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Fixed globe valve ¾ inch class 600 at seal gas line due to gas seeping. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Transfer beam of TEK-3400 welding pad eye 4 point. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Performed housekeeping area. (Done)</p>  <p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Fix the entrance doors due to locking door was loosen and maintenance technical room doors. (Ongoing)</p>  <p>&nbsp;</p>', '<a href="https://pttep-my.sharepoint.com/:f:/r/personal/bongkot_turbine-mech_pttep_com/Documents/2.%20Turbo%20Machine/00%20Shut%20Down%20Job%20%26%20Report/2025.1%20PSD%230%20January%20Shutdown?csf=1&amp;web=1&amp;e=CwSS7S">2025.1 PSD#0 January Shutdown</a>', '2025-09-15 09:08:01', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, 'PTTEP\\Bongkot.Valve', NULL, false, 'G2N') RETURNING id INTO new_report_id;
